  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 125 AM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nDespite Saturday's brief spell of rain and thunder, the outlook for \nthe week ahead remains hot and dry. By Monday, the low-pressure area \nassociated with Saturday's front will move off into the Eastern US, \nand southerly winds will return. Expect a slight delay between that \nswitch and the return of humid Gulf air, giving another day of \nrelatively drier heat on Monday before the region returns to a \nregular routine of hot and humid days with muggy nights. By air \ntemperature, Sunday and Monday are expected to be the hottest days \nof the week with the aid of the drier conditions. \n\nThe elongation of subtropical ridging across the area will secure a \ndry pattern for the week ahead with minimal rain chances. Highs are \nforecast to stay around the upper 90s to low 100s for most of the \narea, with lows in the mid to upper 70s. Continue to practice heat \nsafety and stay cool and hydrated.",
